---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="About" description="About Jasper Japp">
  <!-- Page heading -->
  <div class="mb-8">
    <h1
      class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl"
      style="font-family: var(--font-site);"
    >
      About me
    </h1>
  </div>

  <!-- Two-column layout on lg+: constrained prose left, photos right -->
  <div class="grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_auto] lg:gap-16">
    <!-- Left: prose column, capped at ~70ch -->
    <div class="min-w-0">
      <!-- How I got here -->
      <section class="mb-10" aria-labelledby="how-heading">
        <h2
          id="how-heading"
          class="mb-4 text-lg font-semibold"
          style="font-family: var(--font-site);"
        >
          How I got here
        </h2>
        <div class="app-prose max-w-[70ch]">
          {/* [check] anything wrong or missing? */}
          <p>
            I studied Engineering (Honours) at ANU, majoring in Electronic and
            Communication Systems with a minor in Mechatronics, but most of what
            I learned came from the solar car workshop. I joined ANU Solar Racing
            in 2022 on the aero team, made updates to SC3, built a battery
            cooling system and a rotating wheel fairing, and raced in the 2023
            World Solar Challenge. For the next car I moved to Structures and led
            the <a href="/projects/solar-car-aero/">aero design</a> from concept
            selection through 1,000+ hours of CFD, then
            <a href="/projects/bulkheads-interfacing/"
              >interfaced every subsystem</a
            > into the carbon shell. For the first time the team did most of the
            carbon in house, so I spent two long stretches in Sydney laying up by
            hand. On the 2025 race I was a strategist in the chase car.
          </p>
          <p>
            My Honours project was <a href="/projects/bushfire-detection/"
              >early bushfire detection</a
            >: unsupervised models running on cheap IoT sensor nodes, trained
            only on what normal air looks like. Since May 2026 I've been at
            AirTrunk as an Engineering Specialist, moving around the business to
            get a taste for the whole lifecycle.
          </p>
          <p>
            Lots of what I'm most proud of came from my time with ANU Solar
            Racing (most of the projects here are things I did on my 2nd
            iteration with the team). New to solar racing? Read <a
              href="/solar-racing/">What is Solar Racing?</a
            > for a quick overview and some more gorgeous shots of this very
            special car.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Outside of engineering -->
      <section class="mb-10" aria-labelledby="outside-heading">
        <h2
          id="outside-heading"
          class="mb-4 text-lg font-semibold"
          style="font-family: var(--font-site);"
        >
          Outside of engineering
        </h2>
        <div class="app-prose max-w-[70ch]">
          <p>
            I feel as though I have an almost endless stream of hobbies. I love
            pulling a great shot of espresso. Skiing is one of my favourite
            things when I can get to the mountains. Been experimenting with some
            film photography. And I've started swimming to stay fit. I also
            always have a few projects on the go to keep me busy whether it's
            this website or something to help me learn.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- CV download -->
      <div class="mt-2">
        <a
          href="/JasperJapp_CV.pdf"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg border border-accent/40 bg-accent/5 px-5 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium text-accent no-underline transition-colors hover:border-accent/70 hover:bg-accent/10 focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-accent focus-visible:outline-dashed"
          style="font-family: var(--font-site);"
        >
          View CV
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Right: photos (stacks on mobile, row on sm, right column on lg+) -->
    <aside
      class="flex flex-col gap-6 sm:flex-row sm:flex-wrap sm:gap-6 lg:w-72 lg:flex-col xl:w-80"
      aria-label="Photos"
    >
      <figure class="m-0 flex-1 lg:flex-none">
        <div
          class="overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-border"
          style="aspect-ratio: 3/2;"
        >
          <img
            src="/images/me/Profile.jpg"
            alt="Jasper Japp"
            class="h-full w-full object-cover"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </div>
      </figure>

      <figure class="m-0 flex-1 lg:mt-8 lg:flex-none">
        <div
          class="overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-border"
          style="aspect-ratio: 3/2;"
        >
          <img
            src="/images/me/speaking.jpg"
            alt="Presenting the solar car"
            class="h-full w-full object-cover"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </div>
        {/* [check] where and when? */}
        <figcaption class="mt-2 t-label">Presenting Monty</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <figure class="m-0 flex-1 lg:flex-none">
        <div
          class="overflow-hidden rounded-xl border border-border"
          style="aspect-ratio: 3/2;"
        >
          <img
            src="/images/solar/racing/cattle grids.jpg"
            alt="The solar car crossing a cattle grid"
            class="h-full w-full object-cover"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
          />
        </div>
        <figcaption class="mt-2 t-label">
          Monty on a cattle grid, BWSC 2025
        </figcaption>
      </figure>

      <!-- Now: sits on its own line under the photos on sm, in the rail on lg+ -->
      <div class="sm:basis-full lg:mt-8 lg:basis-auto">
        <h2
          class="text-lg font-semibold"
          style="font-family: var(--font-site);"
        >
          Now
        </h2>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-foreground/85">
          Engineering Specialist at AirTrunk, Sydney, since May 2026.
        </p>
        {/* [check] wording */}
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-foreground/85">
          Side project: Project Raven, a compact wireless comms build that has
          pulled me into PCB design. Ongoing, when it works.
        </p>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div>
</Layout>
